        "original_id": "8e2eda2b-4661-54f0-99a9-b663d7870517",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincent Knesevich de Szent-Helena, Meinhard II (Duke of Carinthia)\n- Places: County of Gorizia and Gradisca, Austria-Hungary\n- Topics: Territorial rule, military occupation, imperial status\n\nFacts:\n- Meinhard II, Duke of Carinthia, once ruled the County of Gorizia and Gradisca together with his brother.\n- In 1805, Vincent Knesevich de Szent-Helena had troops march into the County of Gorizia and Gradisca.\n- In 1867, the County of Gorizia and Gradisca became a crown land of Austria-Hungary.",
